Here-document (<<) is a way to give multiple lines of input to a Linux command.

Think of it like:

“I want to give this whole block of text to a command.”

Basic example

cat << EOF
Hello Bilal
Welcome to Linux
Today I am learning Here Documents
EOF

Output:

Hello Bilal
Welcome to Linux
Today I am learning Here Documents

=> How does it work?
cat << EOF
Hello Bilal
Welcome to Linux
EOF

Explanation:-
cat → command that reads input
<< → tells Bash to start a here-document
EOF → marks the beginning and end
Text between the two EOFs → input given to cat

You can actually use any matching word instead of EOF:

cat << END
Line 1
Line 2
Line 3
END
